====== TP-Link TL-MR12U ======

{{section>meta:infobox:432_warning#infobox_for_dataentries&noheader&nofooter&noeditbutton}}

A [[#Tags|portable_router]] with an onboard 5200mAh battery. See also [[toh:tp-link:tl-mr10u|TL-MR10U]], [[toh:tp-link:tl-mr11u|TL-MR11U]],  [[toh:tp-link:tl-mr13u|TL-MR13U]] or [[toh:tp-link:TL-MR3020]], [[toh:tp-link:TL-MR3040]] and [[toh:tp-link:TL-WR703N]].

**''Note:''** Many of these routers are marketed as a //"3G travel router"// but  **none actually include a 3G modem** - the marketing term rather means that the OEM firmware supports USB 3G modems because it contains drivers for USB modems! Ignore that, because with OpenWrt ANY router with USB supports 3G hardware... ;-)

{{media:tplink:tl-mr12u:tl-mr12u.jpg?400x300|}}

Price: AliExpress - [[http://www.aliexpress.com/wholesale?SearchText=tl-mr12u|about 35 USD]]


